[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5254030397","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122067#issuecomment-5254030397","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122067","id":5254030397,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOSokPQ","user":{"login":"CodeForBeauty","id":121430182,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzzgpg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121430182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeForBeauty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-11T13:47:07Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T13:47:07Z","body":"It seems like the hdr functionality hasn't been added into compatibility renderer.\n\nFrom inspecting the editor in RenderDoc I see that with compatibility the clear color before rendering the scene doesn't get converted from srgb into linear. Whereas with forward plus it does.\n\nScene rendered with Compatibility:\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"862\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/387abb3b-e568-4dd0-8c08-16a152684401\" />\n\nScene rendered with Forward plus:\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"863\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/333dd8e0-ea56-49eb-b900-34f1a18c2f21\" />\n\nWhen the editor is drawn it's colors are also not converted into linear.\n\nEditor rendered with Compatibility:\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"864\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c6927602-f50d-4f60-8444-e94fc6326dec\" />\n\nEditor rendered with Forward plus:\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"864\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed074301-5d1b-4cd2-8555-a68fb1773b19\" />\n\nThe alpha value of the scene render accumulates in Compatibility due to the cleared color of the background having alpha of 1. When this rendered texture is drawn in editor there is some blending involved that uses alpha value. So the output produces incorrect colors.\n\nThe post processing draw call in forward plus seems to have additional code that makes the final render brighter when hdr is enabled. I haven't looked into it fully yet.  But Compatibility doesn't have that.\n\nAdditionally the scene rendering in Compatibility seems to not match Forward plus. In Forward plus the entire scene seems to be drawn darker no matter if hdr is enabled or not. That darker scene is than tone mapped into brighter color if hdr is not enabled. Compatibility doesn't have this step at all.\n\nScene rendered with hdr 2D disabled:\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"861\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f715b2eb-b371-4264-9a53-fa410c847641\" />\n\nAfter tone mapping:\n\n<img width=\"1919\" height=\"865\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64e10902-ded2-4866-b79e-c369fe9e40a9\" />\n\nI'm not super familiar with the engine yet. But if no one is working on this issue yet, I would like to work on this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5254030397/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5308848754","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122067#issuecomment-5308848754","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122067","id":5308848754,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPG6acg","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-16T17:55:41Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T17:55:41Z","body":"I can confirm this with the provided MRP:\n\nHDR 2D disabled | HDR 2D enabled\n--|--\n<img width=\"3839\" height=\"2068\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04166404-85e1-49b0-a13c-7011c97fc680\" />|<img width=\"3839\" height=\"2070\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ea3897ed-fbd2-4e59-9273-ccd1ae7493d6\" />\n\nMy system is:\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 61.64 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\nHere's a couple of screenshots with different `WorldEnvironment` background colours:\n\n`#511345`|`#565656`|`#000000`\n--|--|--\n<img width=\"1478\" height=\"1156\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79e68097-d8fb-4914-bc09-840a507f3f32\" /> | <img width=\"1475\" height=\"1137\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4242a149-b0bf-4e9e-a58e-df61de80acd7\" />|<img width=\"1475\" height=\"1118\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ab434800-2297-4d2a-9dea-54e093dabedf\" />\n\nNot sure if it has to do with how background colours are being mixed in, but hopefully that helps in debugging this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5308848754/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]